WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.933
The ReAct pattern.

2
00:00:02.233 --> 00:00:03.373
Reason, then act.

3
00:00:03.373 --> 00:00:08.000
It is the simplest way to understand what an agent is doing, and why.

4
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.300
ReAct stands for reason plus act.

5
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.056
Before every tool call, the model verbalizes a thought.

6
00:00:15.056 --> 00:00:21.967
That text is scratch computation it can condition on, and it measurably improves tool selection and arguments.

7
00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:24.167
Here is the loop.

8
00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:27.633
First, a thought: what do I know, and what do I still need?

9
00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:29.967
Then an action, which is a tool call.

10
00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:33.197
Then an observation, the result that comes back.

11
00:00:33.197 --> 00:00:36.067
Repeat until the model can give a final answer.

12
00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:38.567
Here's a real trace.

13
00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:42.400
The agent thinks it needs the weekly feed, and calls that tool.

14
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.500
It observes sixty one objects, three hazardous.

15
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.467
New thought: fetch details of the largest one.

16
00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:51.733
The observation says about a hundred sixty meters.

17
00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.533
Now it has enough, and gives the final answer.

18
00:00:55.733 --> 00:01:00.633
Modern APIs bake actions and observations into native tool calling.

19
00:01:00.933 --> 00:01:04.700
But the pattern survives as your mental model for reading traces.

20
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.533
Here's ReAct earning its keep.

21
00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:13.033
A user asks about storms this week, and the agent calls the wrong tool, for Earth events.

22
00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:17.133
The thought line tells you why: it read storms as natural events.

23
00:01:17.433 --> 00:01:23.300
So you rewrite the space-weather tool description to mention geomagnetic storms and solar flares.

24
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.233
The temptation is to guess, and add more prompting.

25
00:01:27.533 --> 00:01:28.985
Instead, read the thoughts.

26
00:01:28.985 --> 00:01:31.833
They show exactly where its understanding went wrong.

27
00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:33.828
Let's recap.

28
00:01:33.828 --> 00:01:37.800
Thought, action, observation, repeated until a final answer.

29
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.067
Thinking first improves tool use.

30
00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:42.367
Traces make agents debuggable.

31
00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.767
So fix the cause, not the prompt.

32
00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:46.167
Next up: tool calling.
